meta {
  name: Get Sold Context
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sold-deals/context?leadId={{createdLeadId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  leadId: {{createdLeadId}}
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns the wizard header", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("leadId");
    expect(body).to.have.property("primaryContactName");
    expect(body).to.have.property("householdId");
    expect(body).to.have.property("householdName");
    expect(body).to.have.property("leadStatus");
  });

  test("returns the household contacts the driver picker offers", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().contacts).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /sold-deals/context — the wizard's header + driver picker (PAC-40)

  What `/sold/new` needs on mount: who the sale is for, and which household
  members can be named as defensive drivers on Card 5.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits`
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:read`
  - **Data scope:** `own` producers only see their own lead; anyone else's is a 404

  ## Why `householdId` can be `null`
  A sale is recorded against a household, and `POST /sold-deals` returns `409`
  for a lead with none. This endpoint reports the gap as `householdId: null`
  **instead of erroring**, so the page can block up front rather than letting a
  producer fill in seven cards and fail at submit.

  The household is resolved with the same self-healing lookup the Quote Recap
  form uses: the migration writes only `legacyHouseholdId` on leads, so the
  fallback repairs `lead.householdId` the first time a migrated lead is touched.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "leadId": "665f…ac1",
    "primaryContactName": "Robin Nakamura",
    "householdId": "665f…b02",
    "householdName": "Nakamura Household",
    "contacts": [
      { "id": "665f…c10", "firstName": "Robin", "lastName": "Nakamura", "roleInHousehold": "Primary" }
    ],
    "leadStatus": "Quoted"
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — malformed `leadId`.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `deal_audits` disabled, or missing `deal_audits:read`.
  - `404 Not Found` — unknown lead, or one outside the caller's data scope.

  ## Ordering
  Run **Leads/Create Lead** first — it sets `createdLeadId`.
}
